    let result=null,audit=null,knownFailure=false,stage=0,selected=0,epoch=1;
    const stages=[
      ['From repairing a view to asking a question','A richer view cannot resolve every gap. Here the world has four components and exactly two are required. A supplied AND-only diagnostic tree proposes an answer, but checking all compatible AND/XOR explanations can reveal action disagreement.','Next: meet the possible worlds'],
      ['Twelve worlds, six possible actions','The installed library has two response models and six possible required sets: twelve represented worlds. Queries return one bit. The policy sees only those responses and supplied operational information; the simulator’s actual required set remains separate.','Next: run the inherited route'],
      ['Notice the action disagreement','Run the diagnostic episode. At the end of the supplied AND-only route, the wider model support may still require different actions. The trace slider lets you inspect that point before additional enquiry. Empty support also requires a hold.','Next: inspect the constructed enquiry'],
      ['Ask what separates the actions','A supplied compiler ranks queries by action-pair separation, balance and price. It checks the resulting enquiry tree against every compatible represented world. New observations narrow support; a model-unanimous required set still needs refresh, a current receipt, permission and a continuing watch.','Next: try a world outside the library'],
      ['A confident model can omit reality','Switch the simulator to the OR mechanism. It is not in the installed library. Some episodes confidently propose the wrong set. Run the trusted audit to expose a contradiction and hold subsequent receiving use. Acquiring a missing expression is the next milestone; it is not installed automatically here.','Return to the introduction']
    ];
    container.innerHTML=`
      <section class="intro"><div><div class="chapter">Encounter 03 · constructive enquiry</div><h1>Ask What Matters</h1><p>When compatible explanations require different actions, construct a question that separates them. Then test the boundary where an internally sufficient answer can still be wrong.</p></div><div class="intro-note">Four components.<br>Two required.<br>Questions, duties and permission.</div></section>
      <section class="guided-path" aria-label="Enquiry guided experience"><div class="guide-top"><span class="chapter" id="enquiry-guide-count"></span><span class="helper">Dotted terms explain the mathematics and link to the publications.</span></div><div class="guide-steps" id="enquiry-guide-steps"></div><h2 id="enquiry-guide-title"></h2><p id="enquiry-guide-description"></p><div class="guide-actions"><button class="secondary" id="enquiry-back" type="button">Previous stage</button><button class="primary" id="enquiry-next" type="button"></button><button class="quiet" id="enquiry-glossary" type="button">Browse all definitions</button></div></section>
      <div class="workspace"><aside class="controls enquiry-controls" aria-label="Enquiry controls"><div class="control-intro"><h2>Try a diagnostic route</h2><p class="helper">The installed library stays AND/XOR.</p></div>
        <label class="field" for="enquiry-route">Diagnostic route<select id="enquiry-route">${Q.ROUTES.map(r=>`<option value="${r.id}">${escape(r.title)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label>
        <label class="field" for="enquiry-budget">Runtime tick budget<select id="enquiry-budget">${[0,3,6,9,12,18,30,48].map(n=>`<option value="${n}" ${n===18?'selected':''}>${n} ticks</option>`).join('')}</select></label>
        <label class="field" for="enquiry-price">Query price<select id="enquiry-price"><option value="unit">1 operation unit per query</option><option value="width">1 operation unit per selected component</option></select></label>
        <label class="toggle-row permission-toggle"><span><strong>Current receiving permission</strong><small>Starts off. A constructed question or justified answer cannot grant it.</small></span><input type="checkbox" id="enquiry-permission" aria-label="Current receiving permission for enquiry"></label>
        <div class="control-buttons"><button class="primary wide-button" id="enquiry-run" type="button">Run diagnostic episode</button><button class="quiet wide-button" id="enquiry-reset" type="button">Reset diagnostic fixture</button><p class="live-note" id="enquiry-status"></p></div>
        <details class="assumptions" id="enquiry-assumptions"><summary>Environment and boundary probes</summary><p class="helper">These truth settings belong to the simulator. The diagnostic policy never reads them.</p>
          <label class="field" for="enquiry-mode">Actual response mechanism<select id="enquiry-mode"><option value="AND">AND · inside the library</option><option value="XOR" selected>XOR · inside the library</option><option value="OR">OR · absent from the library</option></select></label>
          <label class="field" for="enquiry-required">Actual required set<select id="enquiry-required">${Q.SETS.map(K=>`<option value="${K}" ${K===5?'selected':''}>${Q.setName(K)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label>
          <label class="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" id="enquiry-query" aria-label="Query permission" checked><span>Query permission</span></label>
          <label class="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" id="enquiry-refresh" aria-label="Dependency refresh permission" checked><span>Dependency refresh permission</span></label>
          <label class="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" id="enquiry-watch" aria-label="Service continuing watch" checked><span>Service continuing watch on every third tick</span></label>
          <label class="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" id="enquiry-stale" aria-label="Change source version after qualification"><span>Change source version after qualification</span></label>
        </details></aside>
        <div class="working-area"><div class="metrics" aria-live="polite"><div class="metric"><div class="metric-name">Required sets at episode end</div><div class="metric-value" id="enquiry-actions">6</div><div class="metric-detail">Action disagreement, not a safety score</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="metric-name">Queries completed</div><div class="metric-value" id="enquiry-query-count">—</div><div class="metric-detail">Initial route and new enquiry</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="metric-name">Decision tick / deadline</div><div class="metric-value" id="enquiry-deadline">— / 18</div><div class="metric-detail">Every third tick belongs to the watch</div></div></div>
          <section class="context-map enquiry-support"><div class="map-header"><div><h2>What is still compatible?</h2><p id="enquiry-support-caption"></p></div><span class="map-label">Installed: AND / XOR</span></div><div class="hypothesis-grid" id="enquiry-worlds"></div><div class="trace-control"><label for="enquiry-trace">Inspect observations after query <strong id="enquiry-trace-value">0</strong></label><input id="enquiry-trace" type="range" min="0" max="0" value="0" disabled><p id="enquiry-trace-caption"></p></div></section>
          <div class="state-explanation" id="enquiry-explanation" aria-live="polite"></div>
          <section class="panel research-note"><h2>Read-only questions and received answers</h2><div id="enquiry-observations"></div><p class="helper">Noiseless responses and known cardinality are supplied premises. The actual required set is not passed into support reconstruction, query selection or tree qualification.</p></section>
        </div></div>
      <div class="lower-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>How questions narrow the action gap</h2><p>Solid blue: compatible required sets. Dashed green: represented worlds. A single action can be sufficient without unique mechanism identity; zero support requires a hold.</p><div id="enquiry-progress"></div><div class="axis-note">Horizontal: completed queries. Vertical: remaining possibilities. The selected trace point is marked.</div></section>
        <section class="panel"><h2>Why this question?</h2><p>The query score counts separated pairs requiring different actions, then balance, price and mask order. The highest-ranked question heads the constructed plan.</p><div id="enquiry-rank"></div><details class="trace"><summary>Inspect the qualified question plan</summary><p id="enquiry-qualification"></p><pre class="policy-code" id="enquiry-tree" data-no-terms></pre></details></section></div>
      <section class="panel research-note"><h2>A deadline includes continuing duties</h2><p>The complete runtime window remains visible after an early answer or a hold. Every third tick is a watch tick. Compiler development and represented-world qualification are separate from this simulated runtime deadline.</p><div class="tick-legend"><span>Q · query</span><span>R · refresh</span><span>C · receipt qualification</span><span>A · receiving check</span><span>W · watch</span><span>· · idle</span></div><div class="tick-grid" id="enquiry-ticks"></div><p id="enquiry-watch-summary"></p><div class="work-counters" id="enquiry-work"></div></section>
      <section class="panel research-note"><h2>Matched finite comparison</h2><p id="enquiry-census-caption"></p><div class="note-grid"><div><h3>Inside the represented family · 12 episodes</h3><div id="enquiry-main-census"></div></div><div><h3>Outside the library · 6 separate OR episodes</h3><div id="enquiry-stress-census"></div></div></div><div class="census-legend"><span class="correct-key">Correct admission</span><span class="incorrect-key">Incorrect admission</span><span class="hold-key">Withheld</span></div><p>These are this toy’s exact deterministic populations, not the paper’s larger experimental counts. The comparisons have supplied receiving permission, query/refresh access and serviced watches; they do not change your live permissions.</p></section>
      <section class="panel research-note"><h2>Can the model agree and still be wrong?</h2><p>An OR mechanism is available to the simulator but absent from the installed library. A trusted audit can compare a proposed set with the actual required set. Its feedback is separate from diagnosis.</p><div class="execution-controls"><button class="secondary" id="enquiry-or-example" type="button">Load the OR failure fixture</button><button class="secondary" id="enquiry-audit" type="button" disabled>Run trusted dependency audit</button></div><div class="audit-result" id="enquiry-audit-result"></div><p>Finding a contradiction holds subsequent receiving use in this fixture. It does not automatically install OR, change the construction language, grant permission or erase an earlier incorrect admission. A separate expression-acquisition experiment is needed next.</p></section>
      <section class="panel research-note"><details><summary>How this stage integrates and what it demonstrates</summary><div class="note-grid"><div><h3>Another checked part of the pathway</h3><p>Milestones one and two test repair and method reuse. This stage tests whether new observations can resolve an action gap. All three can run in sequence. The earlier five-bit construction method has a different mathematical scope; the diagnostic compiler here is supplied separately.</p><p>No old evidence, required-set answers or grants enter this episode. The sequence checks the earlier milestone record as provenance, rather than claiming that its rule constructor has become a diagnostic compiler.</p></div><div><h3>Finite scope and explicit limits</h3><p>The model has n=4, c=2, AND/XOR response expressions and fourteen proper nonempty queries. It is an educational reconstruction of §3 in <em>Constructive Enquiry and Acquired Model Extension</em>, PDF pp. 1–2. Release duties and residual coverage limits are discussed on pp. 2 and 5–8.</p><p>The score, grammar, qualifier, cardinality, response channel and audit fixture are supplied. There is no learned expression, new semantic primitive, physical concurrent scheduler, production deployment or general alignment guarantee in this stage.</p></div></div></details></section>`;
    const q=id=>container.querySelector('#'+id),listen=(id,event,fn)=>q(id).addEventListener(event,fn,{signal:abort.signal});
    function observedSupport(){return result?Q.support(result.observations.slice(0,selected)):Q.worlds();}
